{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:49:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2d2bb1d5-4d7d-4a69-ad8d-b8c3204351de', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui",\n  "project_name": "whimsical-agent-names"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R3LzsAdM9YaoGaAqDDrnLH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WPYepM1UvWGZoYwkd52zKS', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R3LzsAdM9YaoGaAqDDrnLH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Agent Names Feature - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nReplace cryptic alphanumeric agent identifiers (like `exec_dir_1`, `dev_mgr_abc123`) with whimsical, memorable, American pop culture-inspired names that are family-friendly and fun.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a name generation system that produces consistent, memorable names for agents\\n2. Display whimsical names prominently in the UI while keeping technical IDs available for debugging\\n3. Ensure names are deterministic - same agent ID always maps to the same whimsical name\\n\\n## Design Decisions (Pre-Made)\\n\\n### Name Format\\nNames will follow the pattern: **[Adjective] [Noun]**\\n\\nExamples:\\n- \\"Cheerful Penguin\\"\\n- \\"Cosmic Astronaut\\"  \\n- \\"Mighty Unicorn\\"\\n- \\"Jazzy Robot\\"\\n- \\"Groovy Panda\\"\\n\\n### Word Lists - American Pop Culture Theme\\n**Adjectives** (family-friendly, upbeat):\\n- Cosmic, Groovy, Jazzy, Mighty, Stellar, Radical, Tubular, Gnarly, Bodacious, Wicked\\n- Fantastic, Amazing, Super, Ultra, Mega, Epic, Legendary, Awesome, Marvelous, Incredible\\n- Sparkly, Nifty, Snazzy, Zippy, Zesty, Funky, Peppy, Perky, Chipper, Spunky\\n- Rockin\', Jammin\', Kickin\', Swingin\', Cruisin\', Chillin\', Vibin\', Rollin\', Bouncin\', Groovin\'\\n\\n**Nouns** (pop culture icons, characters, objects):\\n- Astronaut, Robot, Unicorn, Wizard, Ninja, Pirate, Superhero, Viking, Cowboy, Samurai\\n- Panda, Penguin, Phoenix, Dragon, Tiger, Eagle, Falcon, Wolf, Bear, Lion\\n- Rockstar, DJ, Dancer, Magician, Acrobat, Champion, Hero, Legend, Maverick, Ace\\n- Comet, Meteor, Galaxy, Nebula, Supernova, Stardust, Moonbeam, Sunray, Rainbow, Thunder\\n\\n### Implementation Approach\\n1. **Frontend utility function** in JavaScript that:\\n   - Takes an agent ID string\\n   - Hashes it deterministically\\n   - Uses the hash to select adjective and noun from word lists\\n   - Returns the whimsical name\\n\\n2. **UI Integration**:\\n   - Display whimsical name as the primary identifier\\n   - Show technical ID in smaller/muted text or tooltip\\n   - Apply in these components:\\n     - `AgentHierarchyTree.jsx` - tree view of agents\\n     - `AgentStatusPane.jsx` - detailed agent view\\n     - `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` - summary cards\\n     - `ActivityFeed.jsx` - activity entries\\n\\n### Visual Design\\n- Whimsical name: Bold, primary text color\\n- Technical ID: Small, muted gray, shown below or in parentheses\\n- Optional: Add emoji based on agent type (e.g., \\ud83d\\udc51 for executive, \\ud83d\\udd27 for developer)\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### New Files\\n1. `frontend/src/utils/whimsicalNames.js` - Name generation utility\\n\\n### Modified Files\\n1. `frontend/src/components/AgentHierarchyTree.jsx` - Use whimsical names\\n2. `frontend/src/components/AgentStatusPane.jsx` - Use whimsical names\\n3. `frontend/src/components/AgentSummaryPane.jsx` - Use whimsical names\\n4. `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx` - Use whimsical names\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 All agent identifiers display whimsical names in the UI\\n2. \\u2705 Names are deterministic (same ID = same name every time)\\n3. \\u2705 Technical IDs remain accessible (tooltip or secondary text)\\n4. \\u2705 Names are family-friendly American pop culture references\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests pass\\n6. \\u2705 UI remains functional with no regressions\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Backend changes (names are UI-only display transformation)\\n- Persisting name mappings (calculated on-the-fly from hash)\\n- User customization of names\\n- Agent \\"avatars\\" or icons (beyond simple emojis)\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Must not break existing functionality\\n- Must maintain ability to debug using technical IDs\\n- Names must be consistent across page refreshes\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WPYepM1UvWGZoYwkd52zKS', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "main", "changes": {"staged": [], "unstaged": [], "untracked": ["src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "15dc55cd7e0cba90ab4cc7319c6899ef53c2625a", "message": "V1 Cleanup: Fix bugs, remove unused code, harden security", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "4 minutes ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "15dc55cd7e0cba90ab4cc7319c6899ef53c2625a", "message": "V1 Cleanup: Fix bugs, remove unused code, harden security", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "4 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "084a9e8f01f2a2a09a54d4047dbc9b9ac6db9bc9", "message": "Complete Achievement System Expansion milestone 1: foundation planning, architecture, and task breakdown for 100 DCI and NABBA themed achievements", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "42 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "45b57283cde635a516d868d6bef8c96660a2376d", "message": "Complete milestone 1 planning: Whimsical Name Generator foundation architecture and task breakdown", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "43 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "8d043ba9766733f56edb126e12ec12a5db158e6e", "message": "Add comprehensive agent hierarchy documentation and spawn permissions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "70 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "784833714132d5a2d9def39d867f3446186ee901", "message": "Add Best Practices and Anti-Patterns to all agent definitions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "74 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "ff7c891192831c1bdbe4f42984c309d09dee54cf", "message": "Complete architecture and task breakdown for Milestone 1 - Backend foundation with data models, API endpoints, and event integration", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "2ddb05b1c21ecc6096de9c23fdab54744260248e", "message": "Create milestone plan for Requirements Review & Approval Workflow - 4 milestones covering backend, frontend, agents, and integration", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "8299df2c3d1ac6f2ed7f6c09edfcfb2868cb6325", "message": "Add comprehensive executive director status report and project updates", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "4 hours ago"}, {"hash": "c48ef36479dac94f5044eda60907b37b97ee543c", "message": "Add comprehensive test strategy for state preservation hooks", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "19 hours ago"}, {"hash": "efb5e2e99ba30ca87919d0057f156bf31d4f0543", "message": "Fix useUpdateInterval - remove circular dependency causing infinite loop", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "19 hours ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R7eCXVpBLtg4LFjJBYvxAQ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Whimsical Agent Names - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nReplace cryptic alphanumeric agent identifiers with whimsical, memorable, American pop culture-inspired names that are family-friendly and fun.\n\n## Milestone Structure\n\n### Milestone 1: Core Name Generation Utility (Foundation)\n**Objective**: Create the deterministic name generation utility that transforms agent IDs into whimsical names.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. `frontend/src/utils/whimsicalNames.js` - Core utility with:\n   - Word lists (adjectives and nouns from requirements)\n   - Deterministic hash function for agent IDs\n   - `generateWhimsicalName(agentId)` function\n   - Optional: `getAgentEmoji(agentType)` helper\n\n2. `frontend/src/utils/__tests__/whimsicalNames.test.js` - Unit tests:\n   - Determinism: same ID → same name every time\n   - Coverage: different IDs produce varied names\n   - Edge cases: empty strings, null, special characters\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Function returns consistent names for same input\n- [ ] Names follow "[Adjective] [Noun]" format\n- [ ] All unit tests pass\n- [ ] Word lists contain all items from requirements\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Estimated Effort**: Small\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 2: UI Component Integration\n**Objective**: Integrate whimsical names into all relevant UI components.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. Update `AgentHierarchyTree.jsx` - Display whimsical names in tree view\n2. Update `AgentStatusPane.jsx` - Show whimsical name as primary, technical ID secondary\n3. Update `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` - Use whimsical names in summary cards\n4. Update `ActivityFeed.jsx` - Show whimsical names in activity entries\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] All four components display whimsical names prominently\n- [ ] Technical IDs remain accessible (tooltip or muted secondary text)\n- [ ] Visual styling matches design requirements (bold primary, muted secondary)\n- [ ] Optional emojis based on agent type display correctly\n- [ ] All existing component tests pass\n- [ ] No UI regressions\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Technical Decisions\n- **Hash Algorithm**: Use a simple string hashing function (e.g., djb2 or similar) that works in browser\n- **Word List Storage**: Static arrays in the utility file\n- **No Backend Changes**: All name generation is client-side only\n\n### Risk Assessment\n- **Low Risk**: Frontend-only change with clear scope\n- **Testing Strategy**: Unit tests for utility, integration tests for components\n- **Rollback Plan**: Revert component changes if issues arise\n\n## Timeline Summary\n| Milestone | Description | Effort | Dependencies |\n|-----------|-------------|--------|--------------|\n| 1 | Core Name Generation Utility | Small | None |\n| 2 | UI Component Integration | Medium | M1 |\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. All agent identifiers display whimsical names in the UI\n2. Names are deterministic (same ID = same name every time)\n3. Technical IDs remain accessible for debugging\n4. All existing tests pass\n5. UI remains functional with no regressions\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R7eCXVpBLtg4LFjJBYvxAQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/milestone_plan.md", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017oiZQenqE46LP6Y7xQv4uG', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'whimsical-agent-names'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017oiZQenqE46LP6Y7xQv4uG', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I have a good understanding of the existing code structure and the requirements. Let me create the architecture proposal.", "agent": "System Architect"}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I successfully executed the complete project lifecycle: read requirements, created milestone plan, spawned System Architect for architecture, coordinated with Backend/Frontend/Test Coordinators for ta...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
