ent-names/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Whimsical Agent Names - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nReplace cryptic alphanumeric agent identifiers with whimsical, memorable, American pop culture-inspired names that are family-friendly and fun.\n\n## Milestone Structure\n\n### Milestone 1: Core Name Generation Utility (Foundation)\n**Objective**: Create the deterministic name generation utility that transforms agent IDs into whimsical names.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. `frontend/src/utils/whimsicalNames.js` - Core utility with:\n   - Word lists (adjectives and nouns from requirements)\n   - Deterministic hash function for agent IDs\n   - `generateWhimsicalName(agentId)` function\n   - Optional: `getAgentEmoji(agentType)` helper\n\n2. `frontend/src/utils/__tests__/whimsicalNames.test.js` - Unit tests:\n   - Determinism: same ID → same name every time\n   - Coverage: different IDs produce varied names\n   - Edge cases: empty strings, null, special characters\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Function returns consistent names for same input\n- [ ] Names follow "[Adjective] [Noun]" format\n- [ ] All unit tests pass\n- [ ] Word lists contain all items from requirements\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Estimated Effort**: Small\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 2: UI Component Integration\n**Objective**: Integrate whimsical names into all relevant UI components.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. Update `AgentHierarchyTree.jsx` - Display whimsical names in tree view\n2. Update `AgentStatusPane.jsx` - Show whimsical name as primary, technical ID secondary\n3. Update `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` - Use whimsical names in summary cards\n4. Update `ActivityFeed.jsx` - Show whimsical names in activity entries\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] All four components display whimsical names prominently\n- [ ] Technical IDs remain accessible (tooltip or muted secondary text)\n- [ ] Visual styling matches design requirements (bold primary, muted secondary)\n- [ ] Optional emojis based on agent type display correctly\n- [ ] All existing component tests pass\n- [ ] No UI regressions\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Technical Decisions\n- **Hash Algorithm**: Use a simple string hashing function (e.g., djb2 or similar) that works in browser\n- **Word List Storage**: Static arrays in the utility file\n- **No Backend Changes**: All name generation is client-side only\n\n### Risk Assessment\n- **Low Risk**: Frontend-only change with clear scope\n- **Testing Strategy**: Unit tests for utility, integration tests for components\n- **Rollback Plan**: Revert component changes if issues arise\n\n## Timeline Summary\n| Milestone | Description | Effort | Dependencies |\n|-----------|-------------|--------|--------------|\n| 1 | Core Name Generation Utility | Small | None |\n| 2 | UI Component Integration | Medium | M1 |\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. All agent identifiers display whimsical names in the UI\n2. Names are deterministic (same ID = same name every time)\n3. Technical IDs remain accessible for debugging\n4. All existing tests pass\n5. UI remains functional with no regressions\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R7eCXVpBLtg4LFjJBYvxAQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/milestone_plan.md", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017oiZQenqE46LP6Y7xQv4uG', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'whimsical-agent-names'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017oiZQenqE46LP6Y7xQv4uG', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I have a good understanding of the existing code structure and the requirements. Let me create the architecture proposal.", "agent": "System Architect"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AiKjzg5HDUJ8C2dwuNLeie', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AiKjzg5HDUJ8C2dwuNLeie', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01M3bkwE7ywdhghZ4C2jse3o', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md', 'content': '# Whimsical Agent Names - Architecture Document\n\n## Overview\nThis document describes the architecture for the Whimsical Agent Names feature, which transforms cryptic agent IDs into memorable, family-friendly names.\n\n## Architecture Principles\n1. **Frontend-Only**: No backend changes required; all name generation happens client-side\n2. **Deterministic**: Same agent ID always produces the same whimsical name\n3. **Non-Intrusive**: Technical IDs remain available for debugging\n4. **Performant**: Hash-based lookup is O(1) with minimal memory footprint\n\n## Component Architecture\n\n### New Components\n\n#### `frontend/src/utils/whimsicalNames.js`\nCore utility module for name generation.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    whimsicalNames.js                         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  WORD_LISTS                                                  │\n│  ├── ADJECTIVES: string[]  (40 words)                       │\n│  └── NOUNS: string[]       (40 words)                       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  FUNCTIONS                                                   │\n│  ├── hashString(str): number                                │\n│  │   └── Deterministic hash using djb2 algorithm            │\n│  ├── generateWhimsicalName(agentId): string                 │\n│  │   └── Returns "[Adjective] [Noun]" format                │\n│  └── getAgentEmoji(agentType): string                       │\n│      └── Returns emoji based on agent role                  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Modified Components\n\n#### `AgentHierarchyTree.jsx`\n**Changes**:\n- Import `generateWhimsicalName` utility\n- Replace agent ID display with whimsical name\n- Add tooltip or secondary text showing technical ID\n\n#### `AgentStatusPane.jsx`\n**Changes**:\n- Import `generateWhimsicalName` and `getAgentEmoji`\n- Display whimsical name as primary header\n- Show technical ID in muted text below\n- Optional: Add emoji prefix based on agent type\n\n#### `AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\n**Changes**:\n- Import `generateWhimsicalName`\n- Update card title to show whimsical name\n- Keep technical ID accessible in detail view\n\n#### `ActivityFeed.jsx`\n**Changes**:\n- Import `generateWhimsicalName`\n- Replace agent ID in activity entries with whimsical name\n- Consider showing technical ID in expandable detail\n\n## Data Flow\n\n```\n┌──────────────┐     ┌───────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐\n│   Agent ID   │────▶│ generateWhimsical │────▶│  Whimsical Name  │\n│   (string)   │     │    Name(id)       │     │    (string)      │\n└──────────────┘     └───────────────────┘     └──────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n                     ┌───────────────────┐\n                     │   Hash Function   │\n                     │   (djb2 algo)     │\n                     └───────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n                     ┌───────────────────┐\n                     │  Index Selection  │\n                     │  adj = hash % 40  │\n                     │  noun = hash/40%40│\n                     └───────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Hash Algorithm: djb2\n\nThe djb2 hash is chosen for:\n- Simplicity and speed\n- Good distribution\n- Deterministic results\n- Browser compatibility\n\n```javascript\nfunction hashString(str) {\n  let hash = 5381;\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\n    hash = ((hash << 5) + hash) + str.charCodeAt(i);\n    hash = hash & hash; // Convert to 32-bit integer\n  }\n  return Math.abs(hash);\n}\n```\n\n## Word Lists\n\n### Adjectives (40 words)\nFrom requirements - American pop culture themed:\n- Cosmic, Groovy, Jazzy, Mighty, Stellar, Radical, Tubular, Gnarly, Bodacious, Wicked\n- Fantastic, Amazing, Super, Ultra, Mega, Epic, Legendary, Awesome, Marvelous, Incredible\n- Sparkly, Nifty, Snazzy, Zippy, Zesty, Funky, Peppy, Perky, Chipper, Spunky\n- Rockin, Jammin, Kickin, Swingin, Cruisin, Chillin, Vibin, Rollin, Bouncin, Groovin\n\n### Nouns (40 words)\nFrom requirements - pop culture icons:\n- Astronaut, Robot, Unicorn, Wizard, Ninja, Pirate, Superhero, Viking, Cowboy, Samurai\n- Panda, Penguin, Phoenix, Dragon, Tiger, Eagle, Falcon, Wolf, Bear, Lion\n- Rockstar, DJ, Dancer, Magician, Acrobat, Champion, Hero, Legend, Maverick, Ace\n- Comet, Meteor, Galaxy, Nebula, Supernova, Stardust, Moonbeam, Sunray, Rainbow, Thunder\n\n### Combination Space\n40 adjectives × 40 nouns = 1,600 unique name combinations\n\n## Agent Type Emojis\n\n```javascript\nconst AGENT_EMOJIS = {\n  \'executive_director\': \'👑\',\n  \'development_manager\': \'📋\',\n  \'system_architect\': \'🏗️\',\n  \'tdd_coordinator\': \'🧪\',\n  \'backend_coordinator\': \'⚙️\',\n  \'frontend_coordinator\': \'🎨\',\n  \'test_coordinator\': \'✅\',\n  \'code_writer\': \'💻\',\n  \'code_tester\': \'🔬\',\n  \'section_tech\': \'🔧\',\n  \'section_leader\': \'📊\',\n  \'default\': \'🤖\'\n};\n```\n\n## Visual Design Implementation\n\n### Primary Display Pattern\n```jsx\n<div className="agent-identity">\n  <span className="agent-emoji">{emoji}</span>\n  <span className="agent-name">{whimsicalName}</span>\n  <span className="agent-id-secondary">({technicalId})</span>\n</div>\n```\n\n### CSS Considerations\n```css\n.agent-name {\n  font-weight: bold;\n  color: var(--text-primary);\n}\n\n.agent-id-secondary {\n  font-size: 0.85em;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  margin-left: 0.5em;\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests (whimsicalNames.test.js)\n1. **Determinism Test**: Same input always produces same output\n2. **Format Test**: Output matches "[Adjective] [Noun]" pattern\n3. **Distribution Test**: Different inputs produce different outputs\n4. **Edge Cases**: Empty string, null, undefined, special characters\n5. **Emoji Mapping**: Correct emojis for each agent type\n\n### Component Tests\n1. Verify whimsical names render correctly\n2. Verify technical IDs remain accessible\n3. Verify no regressions in existing functionality\n4. Verify emoji display for different agent types\n\n## Performance Considerations\n- Hash calculation: O(n) where n is string length (typically < 50 chars)\n- Word list lookup: O(1) array index access\n- Memory: ~2KB for word lists (static, loaded once)\n- No caching needed due to fast hash calculation\n\n## File Structure\n```\nfrontend/src/\n├── utils/\n│   ├── whimsicalNames.js          # NEW\n│   └── __tests__/\n│       └── whimsicalNames.test.js # NEW\n├── components/\n│   ├── AgentHierarchyTree.jsx     # MODIFIED\n│   ├── AgentStatusPane.jsx        # MODIFIED\n│   ├── AgentSummaryPane.jsx       # MODIFIED\n│   └── ActivityFeed.jsx           # MODIFIED\n```\n\n## Integration Points\n- Components import from `../utils/whimsicalNames.js`\n- No backend integration required\n- No state management changes needed\n- No routing changes required\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|\n| Name collisions | 1,600 combinations is sufficient for typical agent counts |\n| Hash inconsistency across browsers | djb2 uses only basic JS operations |\n| Breaking existing tests | Update tests to expect new name format |\n| Performance impact | Hash is O(n) and very fast |\n\n## Future Considerations (Out of Scope)\n- User-customizable names\n- Persistent name mappings\n- Avatar/icon system\n- Name preferences/themes\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01M3bkwE7ywdhghZ4C2jse3o', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01JvhrNCis3uaEKYGragxBSb', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Milestone 1: Core Name Generation Utility - Create the deterministic whimsicalNames.js utility with word lists, djb2 hash function, generateWhimsicalName(agentId) function, and getAgentEmoji(agentType) helper', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015KDXDyvkSrkAhTcsaRJ5EC', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/test_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Milestone 1: Core Name Generation Utility - Create unit tests for whimsicalNames.js covering determinism, format validation, distribution, edge cases, and emoji mapping', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/test_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JvhrNCis3uaEKYGragxBSb', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 5, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 (Word Lists) \\u2192 Task 3 (Generate Name)", "Task 2 (Hash Function) \\u2192 Task 3 (Generate Name)", "Task 4 (Get Emoji) \\u2192 Independent", "Tasks 1-4 \\u2192 Task 5 (Exports & Documentation)"], "message": "Successfully created frontend task breakdown for Milestone 1. Identified 5 tasks for implementing the core whimsicalNames.js utility: (1) Word list constants with 40 adjectives and 40 nouns, (2) djb2 hash function for deterministic ID hashing, (3) generateWhimsicalName function for \'[Adjective] [Noun]\' output, (4) getAgentEmoji helper for agent type emojis, and (5) module exports with JSDoc documentation. All tasks are pure JavaScript utilities with no UI dependencies, making them ideal for TDD implementation. The utility provides 1,600 unique name combinations and is ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for red-green-refactor development cycles."}}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015KDXDyvkSrkAhTcsaRJ5EC', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I\'ll analyze the requirements and architecture to create a comprehensive test strategy for Milestone 1 focusing on the core utility `whimsicalNames.js`.", "agent": "Test Coordinator"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DJoWxkYymji5iBQy1juUie', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V4aWqLrzqMCdoyJn1dBECi', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DJoWxkYymji5iBQy1juUie', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Tasks - Milestone 1: Core Name Generation Utility\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis milestone focuses on creating the core `whimsicalNames.js` utility module with deterministic name generation capabilities. This is a pure JavaScript utility with no UI dependencies, making it ideal for TDD implementation.\\n\\n## Architecture Context\\n- **Location**: `frontend/src/utils/whimsicalNames.js`\\n- **Purpose**: Transform agent IDs into whimsical, memorable names\\n- **Approach**: Hash-based deterministic selection from curated word lists\\n- **Dependencies**: None (pure JavaScript utility)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Breakdown\\n\\n### Task 1: Create Word List Constants\\n**Priority**: High (Foundation)  \\n**Complexity**: Simple  \\n**Estimated Effort**: 30 minutes  \\n\\n**Description**:\\nCreate the ADJECTIVES and NOUNS constant arrays in `whimsicalNames.js` containing the curated word lists from requirements.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- [ ] ADJECTIVES array contains exactly 40 words from requirements\\n- [ ] NOUNS array contains exactly 40 words from requirements\\n- [ ] Words are properly formatted (consistent capitalization)\\n- [ ] Arrays are exported for testing\\n- [ ] All words are family-friendly and match American pop culture theme\\n- [ ] Words maintain order specified in requirements for reproducibility\\n\\n**Word Lists** (from requirements):\\n\\n*Adjectives (40 words)*:\\nCosmic, Groovy, Jazzy, Mighty, Stellar, Radical, Tubular, Gnarly, Bodacious, Wicked, Fantastic, Amazing, Super, Ultra, Mega, Epic, Legendary, Awesome, Marvelous, Incredible, Sparkly, Nifty, Snazzy, Zippy, Zesty, Funky, Peppy, Perky, Chipper, Spunky, Rockin, Jammin, Kickin, Swingin, Cruisin, Chillin, Vibin, Rollin, Bouncin, Groovin\\n\\n*Nouns (40 words)*:\\nAstronaut, Robot, Unicorn, Wizard, Ninja, Pirate, Superhero, Viking, Cowboy, Samurai, Panda, Penguin, Phoenix, Dragon, Tiger, Eagle, Falcon, Wolf, Bear, Lion, Rockstar, DJ, Dancer, Magician, Acrobat, Champion, Hero, Legend, Maverick, Ace, Comet, Meteor, Galaxy, Nebula, Supernova, Stardust, Moonbeam, Sunray, Rainbow, Thunder\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Test Coverage Required**:\\n- Verify exact word count (40 each)\\n- Verify no duplicate words\\n- Verify all words are non-empty strings\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 2: Implement djb2 Hash Function\\n**Priority**: High (Core Algorithm)  \\n**Complexity**: Simple  \\n**Estimated Effort**: 45 minutes  \\n\\n**Description**:\\nImplement the `hashString(str)` function using the djb2 algorithm for deterministic hash generation from agent ID strings.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- [ ] Function accepts string input\\n- [ ] Returns positive integer\\n- [ ] Implements djb2 algorithm correctly (initial hash = 5381, formula: `hash = ((hash << 5) + hash) + charCode`)\\n- [ ] Converts to 32-bit integer using bitwise AND\\n- [ ] Returns absolute value (no negative hashes)\\n- [ ] Same input always produces same output (deterministic)\\n- [ ] Different inputs produce different outputs (good distribution)\\n- [ ] Handles edge cases: empty string, special characters, Unicode\\n\\n**Algorithm Specification** (from architecture):\\n```javascript\\nfunction hashString(str) {\\n  let hash = 5381;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\\n    hash = ((hash << 5) + hash) + str.charCodeAt(i);\\n    hash = hash & hash; // Convert to 32-bit integer\\n  }\\n  return Math.abs(hash);\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Test Coverage Required**:\\n- Determinism: Same input produces same output (test with multiple calls)\\n- Distribution: Different inputs produce different hashes\\n- Edge cases: empty string, null, undefined\\n- Special characters: handle hyphens, underscores, numbers\\n- Unicode: handle emoji and international characters\\n- Type safety: handle non-string inputs gracefully\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 3: Implement generateWhimsicalName Function\\n**Priority**: High (Core Feature)  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Estimated Effort**: 1 hour  \\n\\n**Description**:\\nImplement the main `generateWhimsicalName(agentId)` function that takes an agent ID and returns a whimsical name in \\"[Adjective] [Noun]\\" format.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- [ ] Function accepts agentId string as parameter\\n- [ ] Returns string in format \\"[Adjective] [Noun]\\"\\n- [ ] Uses hashString() to generate hash from agentId\\n- [ ] Selects adjective using modulo: `hash % 40`\\n- [ ] Selects noun using division and modulo: `Math.floor(hash / 40) % 40`\\n- [ ] Same agentId always returns same name (deterministic)\\n- [ ] Different agentIds produce different names (with high probability)\\n- [ ] Handles edge cases: empty string, null, undefined\\n- [ ] Returns fallback name for invalid inputs (e.g., \\"Unknown Agent\\")\\n\\n**Algorithm Specification**:\\n1. Hash the agent ID using `hashString(agentId)`\\n2. Calculate adjective index: `hash % ADJECTIVES.length`\\n3. Calculate noun index: `Math.floor(hash / ADJECTIVES.length) % NOUNS.length`\\n4. Return `${adjective} ${noun}`\\n\\n**Dependencies**: \\n- Task 1 (Word Lists)\\n- Task 2 (Hash Function)\\n\\n**Test Coverage Required**:\\n- Format validation: Output matches \\"[Adjective] [Noun]\\" pattern\\n- Determinism: Same ID produces same name across multiple calls\\n- Distribution: Different IDs produce different names\\n- Edge cases: null, undefined, empty string, whitespace-only\\n- Boundary testing: Very long strings, special characters\\n- Collision testing: Verify hash distribution leads to name variety\\n- Integration: Verify adjective and noun come from correct word lists\\n\\n**Example Expected Outputs**:\\n- `generateWhimsicalName(\\"exec_dir_1\\")` \\u2192 e.g., \\"Cosmic Astronaut\\"\\n- `generateWhimsicalName(\\"dev_mgr_abc123\\")` \\u2192 e.g., \\"Groovy Panda\\"\\n- Names should be different for different IDs but consistent for same ID\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 4: Implement getAgentEmoji Helper Function\\n**Priority**: Medium (Enhancement)  \\n**Complexity**: Simple  \\n**Estimated Effort**: 30 minutes  \\n\\n**Description**:\\nImplement the `getAgentEmoji(agentType)` helper function that returns an appropriate emoji based on agent role/type.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- [ ] Function accepts agentType string as parameter\\n- [ ] Returns single emoji character (string)\\n- [ ] Implements emoji mapping from architecture specification\\n- [ ] Returns default emoji (\\ud83e\\udd16) for unknown agent types\\n- [ ] Handles null/undefined inputs gracefully\\n- [ ] Case-insensitive matching (e.g., \\"executive_director\\" or \\"Executive_Director\\")\\n- [ ] All emoji characters are valid Unicode and display correctly\\n\\n**Emoji Mapping** (from architecture):\\n```javascript\\nconst AGENT_EMOJIS = {\\n  \'executive_director\': \'\\ud83d\\udc51\',\\n  \'development_manager\': \'\\ud83d\\udccb\',\\n  \'system_architect\': \'\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f\',\\n  \'tdd_coordinator\': \'\\ud83e\\uddea\',\\n  \'backend_coordinator\': \'\\u2699\\ufe0f\',\\n  \'frontend_coordinator\': \'\\ud83c\\udfa8\',\\n  \'test_coordinator\': \'\\u2705\',\\n  \'code_writer\': \'\\ud83d\\udcbb\',\\n  \'code_tester\': \'\\ud83d\\udd2c\',\\n  \'section_tech\': \'\\ud83d\\udd27\',\\n  \'section_leader\': \'\\ud83d\\udcca\',\\n  \'default\': \'\\ud83e\\udd16\'\\n};\\n```\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Test Coverage Required**:\\n- Valid agent types: Return correct emoji for each type\\n- Unknown types: Return default emoji (\\ud83e\\udd16)\\n- Edge cases: null, undefined, empty string \\u2192 default emoji\\n- Case insensitivity: Handle mixed case inputs\\n- Type validation: Non-string inputs handled gracefully\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 5: Create Module Exports and Documentation\\n**Priority**: High (Integration)  \\n**Complexity**: Simple  \\n**Estimated Effort**: 30 minutes  \\n\\n**Description**:\\nCreate proper ES6 module exports and JSDoc documentation for all public functions in `whimsicalNames.js`.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- [ ] All public functions exported using named exports\\n- [ ] JSDoc comments for all exported functions\\n- [ ] Parameter types documented with @param\\n- [ ] Return types documented with @return\\n- [ ] Usage examples provided in JSDoc @example tags\\n- [ ] Module-level documentation explaining purpose\\n- [ ] Word lists exported for testing purposes\\n- [ ] Hash function exported (may be useful for debugging)\\n\\n**Export Structure**:\\n```javascript\\nexport {\\n  generateWhimsicalName,\\n  getAgentEmoji,\\n  hashString,        // For testing/debugging\\n  ADJECTIVES,        // For testing\\n  NOUNS              // For testing\\n};\\n```\\n\\n**JSDoc Example**:\\n```javascript\\n/**\\n * Generates a whimsical name from an agent ID using deterministic hash-based selection.\\n * \\n * @param {string} agentId - The technical agent identifier (e.g., \\"exec_dir_1\\")\\n * @returns {string} A whimsical name in \\"[Adjective] [Noun]\\" format\\n * @example\\n * generateWhimsicalName(\\"exec_dir_1\\") // Returns e.g., \\"Cosmic Astronaut\\"\\n */\\n```\\n\\n**Dependencies**: \\n- Task 1 (Word Lists)\\n- Task 2 (Hash Function)\\n- Task 3 (Generate Name)\\n- Task 4 (Get Emoji)\\n\\n**Test Coverage Required**:\\n- Verify all exports are accessible\\n- Verify imports work in test files\\n- Documentation examples should be executable and accurate\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Test File: `frontend/src/utils/__tests__/whimsicalNames.test.js`\\n\\n**Test Suites**:\\n\\n1. **Word Lists Tests**\\n   - Verify ADJECTIVES has 40 words\\n   - Verify NOUNS has 40 words\\n   - Verify no duplicate words in each list\\n   - Verify all words are non-empty strings\\n\\n2. **Hash Function Tests**\\n   - Determinism: Same input \\u2192 same output\\n   - Distribution: Different inputs \\u2192 different outputs\\n   - Edge cases: empty string, null, undefined\\n   - Special characters: handle properly\\n   - Performance: Fast enough for real-time use\\n\\n3. **Generate Name Tests**\\n   - Format: Output matches \\"[Adjective] [Noun]\\"\\n   - Determinism: Same ID \\u2192 same name\\n   - Distribution: Different IDs \\u2192 different names (spot check)\\n   - Edge cases: null, undefined, empty string\\n   - Integration: Uses correct word lists\\n\\n4. **Get Emoji Tests**\\n   - Known types: Return correct emoji\\n   - Unknown types: Return default emoji\\n   - Edge cases: null, undefined, empty string\\n   - Case sensitivity: Handle mixed case\\n\\n5. **Integration Tests**\\n   - Generate 100 different names, verify format\\n   - Check for reasonable distribution (no single name dominates)\\n   - Verify all exported functions work together\\n\\n---\\n\\n## File Structure\\n\\n```\\nfrontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 whimsicalNames.js          # NEW - Main utility module\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 whimsicalNames.test.js # NEW - Unit tests\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Definition of Done\\n\\nThis milestone is complete when:\\n\\n\\u2705 **All 5 tasks implemented and passing tests**\\n\\u2705 **Unit test coverage \\u2265 95% for whimsicalNames.js**\\n\\u2705 **All tests passing with no warnings**\\n\\u2705 **JSDoc documentation complete for all exports**\\n\\u2705 **Code follows project style guidelines (ESLint passes)**\\n\\u2705 **Determinism verified: Same inputs always produce same outputs**\\n\\u2705 **Edge cases handled gracefully**\\n\\u2705 **Module can be imported and used in other files**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n| Risk | Mitigation |\\n|------|------------|\\n| Hash collisions | 40 \\u00d7 40 = 1,600 combinations sufficient for typical agent counts |\\n| Browser compatibility | djb2 uses only basic JS operations supported everywhere |\\n| Performance concerns | Hash is O(n) on string length, very fast for typical agent IDs |\\n| Unicode handling | Use charCodeAt() which handles all valid JS strings |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Next Steps After M1\\n\\nAfter completing this milestone, the utility will be ready for integration into UI components in Milestone 2:\\n- Integrate into `AgentHierarchyTree.jsx`\\n- Integrate into `AgentStatusPane.jsx`\\n- Integrate into `AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n- Integrate into `ActivityFeed.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Notes for TDD Coordinator\\n\\n- **Start with Task 1** (word lists) as it has no dependencies\\n- **Tasks 2-4 can be done in TDD red-green-refactor cycles**\\n- **Task 5** should be done last to document the complete API\\n- **All functions are pure** (no side effects), making them ideal for TDD\\n- **Focus on determinism** - this is critical for user experience\\n- **Edge case handling is important** - don\'t assume valid inputs\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V4aWqLrzqMCdoyJn1dBECi', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/test_tasks_m1.md"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TzwrSrGXh7VLH2EgpT7FsD', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Tasks - Milestone 1: Core Name Generation Utility\n\n## Overview\nThis document outlines the test strategy for the whimsicalNames.js utility module. Tests will follow TDD principles and ensure comprehensive coverage of all functionality.\n\n## Test File Location\n`frontend/src/utils/__tests__/whimsicalNames.test.js`\n\n---\n\n## Test Suite 1: Word Lists Validation\n\n### Test 1.1: ADJECTIVES Array Validation\n**Description**: Verify ADJECTIVES array structure and contents\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] ADJECTIVES array exists and is an array\n- [ ] ADJECTIVES has exactly 40 words\n- [ ] All adjectives are non-empty strings\n- [ ] No duplicate adjectives in the list\n- [ ] All adjectives match words from requirements\n\n### Test 1.2: NOUNS Array Validation\n**Description**: Verify NOUNS array structure and contents\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] NOUNS array exists and is an array\n- [ ] NOUNS has exactly 40 words\n- [ ] All nouns are non-empty strings\n- [ ] No duplicate nouns in the list\n- [ ] All nouns match words from requirements\n\n---\n\n## Test Suite 2: Hash Function (hashString)\n\n### Test 2.1: Determinism\n**Description**: Verify same input always produces same output\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] `hashString("test")` returns same value on multiple calls\n- [ ] `hashString("agent_123")` returns same value on multiple calls\n- [ ] `hashString("exec_dir_abc")` returns same value on multiple calls\n\n### Test 2.2: Output Properties\n**Description**: Verify hash function output characteristics\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] Returns a number\n- [ ] Returns a positive integer\n- [ ] Returns value >= 0 (no negative hashes)\n- [ ] Returns finite number (not Infinity)\n\n### Test 2.3: Distribution\n**Description**: Verify different inputs produce different outputs\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] `hashString("a")` ≠ `hashString("b")`\n- [ ] `hashString("test1")` ≠ `hashString("test2")`\n- [ ] `hashString("agent_1")` ≠ `hashString("agent_2")`\n- [ ] 10 random strings produce 10 different hashes\n\n### Test 2.4: Edge Cases\n**Description**: Verify handling of edge case inputs\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] Empty string returns a valid number\n- [ ] String with only spaces returns a valid number\n- [ ] String with special characters (!, @, #, etc.) works\n- [ ] String with numbers works\n- [ ] Very long strings (1000+ chars) work without error\n- [ ] Unicode characters work correctly\n- [ ] String with emoji works\n\n### Test 2.5: Type Safety\n**Description**: Verify handling of invalid input types\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] null input is handled gracefully (returns number or throws meaningful error)\n- [ ] undefined input is handled gracefully\n- [ ] Number input is handled (converted to string or throws)\n- [ ] Object input is handled gracefully\n\n---\n\n## Test Suite 3: Generate Whimsical Name\n\n### Test 3.1: Output Format\n**Description**: Verify output matches expected format\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] Returns a string\n- [ ] Output contains exactly one space\n- [ ] First word is from ADJECTIVES list\n- [ ] Second word is from NOUNS list\n- [ ] Output matches regex `/^[A-Z][a-z]+ [A-Z][a-z]+$/`\n\n### Test 3.2: Determinism\n**Description**: Verify same agent ID always produces same name\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] `generateWhimsicalName("test")` returns same name on multiple calls\n- [ ] `generateWhimsicalName("agent_123")` returns same name on multiple calls\n- [ ] Same name after page refresh simulation (fresh function call)\n- [ ] 100 calls with same ID produce identical results\n\n### Test 3.3: Distribution\n**Description**: Verify different agent IDs produce different names\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] `generateWhimsicalName("agent_1")` ≠ `generateWhimsicalName("agent_2")`\n- [ ] 100 different agent IDs produce varied names (not all the same)\n- [ ] Sequential IDs (agent_1, agent_2, ..., agent_10) produce 10 different names\n\n### Test 3.4: Edge Cases\n**Description**: Verify handling of edge case inputs\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] Empty string input returns valid name or fallback\n- [ ] null input returns fallback name "Unknown Agent" or similar\n- [ ] undefined input returns fallback name\n- [ ] Very long string input works correctly\n- [ ] String with special characters works\n- [ ] String with only whitespace is handled\n\n### Test 3.5: Integration\n**Description**: Verify integration with word lists and hash function\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] All returned adjectives exist in ADJECTIVES array\n- [ ] All returned nouns exist in NOUNS array\n- [ ] Name generation uses hashString internally\n\n---\n\n## Test Suite 4: Get Agent Emoji\n\n### Test 4.1: Known Agent Types\n**Description**: Verify correct emoji for each known agent type\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("executive_director")` returns "👑"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("development_manager")` returns "📋"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("system_architect")` returns "🏗️"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("tdd_coordinator")` returns "🧪"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("backend_coordinator")` returns "⚙️"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("frontend_coordinator")` returns "🎨"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("test_coordinator")` returns "✅"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("code_writer")` returns "💻"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("code_tester")` returns "🔬"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("section_tech")` returns "🔧"\n- [ ] `getAgentEmoji("section_leader")` returns "📊"\n\n### Test 4.2: Default Emoji\n**Description**: Verify default emoji for unknown types\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] Unknown type "unknown_agent" returns "🤖"\n- [ ] Random string "xyz" returns "🤖"\n- [ ] Empty string returns "🤖"\n\n### Test 4.3: Edge Cases\n**Description**: Verify edge case handling\n**Tests**:\n- [ ] null input returns default emoji "🤖"\n- [ ] undefined input returns default emoji "🤖"\n- [ ] Case insensitive: "Executive_Director" returns "👑"\n- [ ] Case insensitive: "DEVELOPMENT_MANAGER" return