{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:53:08", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a87f336f-30e2-4a80-9cf8-3e5c6845adf5', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 1: Analysis and Architecture - Understand current RecoveryDashboard implementation and identify specific CSS/styling issues causing readability problems",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AQpj5EorJFp7o6c1Mb2dJR', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AQpj5EorJFp7o6c1Mb2dJR', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: British Brass Band Achievements\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis project extends the existing Ensemble achievements system by adding a new \\"BRASS_BAND\\" achievement category. This follows an **extension pattern** - adding new content to an existing, well-structured system without modifying core architecture.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Plugin/Extension pattern for achievement categories\\n**Approach Rationale**: The existing achievements system is well-designed with clear enum-based categories and a list-based achievement registry. We simply extend these existing structures.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Current Stack (Maintained)\\n- **Backend**: Python with typed dataclasses for Achievement models\\n- **Frontend**: React with Bootstrap for UI components\\n- **State Management**: Props-based filtering in React components\\n- **API**: Existing achievement endpoints (no changes needed)\\n\\n### No New Dependencies Required\\nThe existing stack fully supports this extension.\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n**1. AchievementCategory Enum** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Has SKA and other categories\\n- **Change**: Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` enum value\\n\\n**2. ACHIEVEMENTS List** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Contains Achievement objects for existing categories\\n- **Change**: Add 15 new Achievement objects for BRASS_BAND category\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n**3. AchievementsDashboard** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`)\\n- **Filter Dropdown**: Add brass_band option with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n- **getCategoryBadge Function**: Handle brass_band category styling\\n- **Fun Facts Section**: Optionally add brass band trivia\\n\\n### Component Interaction Flow\\n```\\nUser selects \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n    \\u2193\\nAchievementsDashboard filters by category=\\"brass_band\\"\\n    \\u2193\\nAPI returns achievements with category BRASS_BAND\\n    \\u2193\\nUI displays brass band achievements with proper badges\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.py          # MODIFY: Add enum + 15 achievements\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementsDashboard.jsx  # MODIFY: Add filter + badge\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement Object (Existing Pattern)\\n```python\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,  # NEW CATEGORY\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Achievement Definitions (15 Total)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Rarity | Points | Trigger Type |\\n|----|------|--------|--------|--------------|\\n| championship_section | Championship Section | LEGENDARY | 200 | total_executions >= 50 |\\n| silver_band | Silver Band | RARE | 50 | consecutive_successes >= 5 |\\n| principal_cornet | Principal Cornet | UNCOMMON | 30 | sub_agents_led >= 3 |\\n| adjudicator | The Adjudicator | RARE | 60 | test_evaluations >= 25 |\\n| test_piece | Test Piece Mastery | UNCOMMON | 25 | iterations_in_task > 10 |\\n| bandroom_practice | Bandroom Practice | COMMON | 15 | total_executions >= 10 |\\n| promotion | Section Promotion | EPIC | 100 | success_rate_improvement |\\n| brass_section_harmony | Brass Section Harmony | RARE | 45 | concurrent_completions |\\n| march_on_stage | March on Stage | COMMON | 10 | first_task_in_project |\\n| quick_march | Quick March | RARE | 40 | task_time < 10s |\\n| hymn_tune_encore | Hymn Tune Encore | UNCOMMON | 35 | recovery_from_failure |\\n| grand_shield | Grand Shield | EPIC | 120 | consecutive_successes >= 25 |\\n| fanfare | Fanfare | RARE | 55 | achievements_in_session >= 5 |\\n| youth_band_graduate | Youth Band Graduate | UNCOMMON | 20 | new_agent_first_10_tasks |\\n| national_finals | National Finals | LEGENDARY | 150 | project_completion |\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API Changes Required**\\n- Existing `/api/achievements` endpoint supports category filtering\\n- Frontend already handles dynamic category data\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Backend Testing\\n1. Verify BRASS_BAND enum exists\\n2. Verify 15 achievements load without errors\\n3. Verify achievement triggering works\\n4. Run existing achievement test suite\\n\\n### Frontend Testing\\n1. Verify brass_band filter appears in dropdown\\n2. Verify filter functionality works\\n3. Verify badge displays correctly\\n4. Verify no console errors\\n\\n### Manual Verification\\n- Load AchievementsDashboard\\n- Select \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n- Verify achievements display with correct icons/badges\\n- Verify at least one achievement can trigger\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend (achievements.py)\\n1. Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to AchievementCategory enum\\n2. Add 15 Achievement objects to ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. Verify file imports correctly\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend (AchievementsDashboard.jsx)\\n1. Add brass_band to category filter dropdown\\n2. Update getCategoryBadge function\\n3. Optionally add fun facts\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Integration Testing\\n1. Run existing tests\\n2. Manual verification\\n3. Commit changes\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Trigger Condition Compatibility\\n**Impact**: New trigger conditions might not work with existing tracker\\n**Mitigation**: Use only existing trigger condition types\\n\\n### Risk 2: Frontend Filter Inconsistency\\n**Impact**: Filter might not match backend category name\\n**Mitigation**: Ensure exact string match \\"brass_band\\"\\n\\n## Key Implementation Decisions\\n\\n1. **Enum Value**: Use `brass_band` (lowercase with underscore) matching existing pattern\\n2. **Icon**: Use \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary icon since cornet emoji unavailable\\n3. **Trigger Conditions**: Reuse existing types, no new event tracking\\n4. **Points Range**: Follow existing scale based on rarity\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. \\u2705 BRASS_BAND in AchievementCategory enum\\n2. \\u2705 15 achievements in ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. \\u2705 brass_band filter works in UI\\n4. \\u2705 getCategoryBadge handles brass_band\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests pass\\n6. \\u2705 No console errors in frontend\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FeN7sfn17StyuDovxKRtkh', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FeN7sfn17StyuDovxKRtkh', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Readability Fix - Improve Page\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Vision**: Fix the unreadable text on the \\"Improve\\" page (SelfImprovementDashboard component) where black text appears on dark backgrounds, making it nearly impossible to read.\\n\\n**Problem**: Users report that the Improve page has severe readability issues with black text on dark backgrounds, creating a poor user experience and making the interface unusable in some areas.\\n\\n**Solution**: Identify and fix all instances of poor contrast between text and background colors to ensure proper readability across all UI elements.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Core Requirements\\n1. **Readability Fix**: Ensure all text on the Improve page is readable with proper contrast\\n2. **Bootstrap Consistency**: Maintain Bootstrap theme consistency while fixing contrast issues\\n3. **Dark Mode Compatibility**: Ensure fixes work properly in both light and dark mode contexts\\n4. **Accessibility**: Meet WCAG guidelines for text contrast (minimum 4.5:1 ratio for normal text)\\n\\n### Specific Issues to Address\\n1. **Card Backgrounds**: Review all Card components with `bg=\\"dark\\"` and ensure text is white/light\\n2. **Alert Styling**: Ensure Alert components have proper text contrast\\n3. **Badge Colors**: Verify Badge components maintain readability\\n4. **Auto-Apply Toggle**: Check styling of the toggle switch and associated text\\n5. **Table Content**: Ensure table text is readable against backgrounds\\n6. **Modal Content**: Verify modal text readability\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing Bootstrap theme\\n- Cannot break existing functionality\\n- Must preserve current color scheme intent (danger/warning/success indicators)\\n- Should use Bootstrap\'s built-in text color classes where possible\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. All text on the Improve page is readable with adequate contrast\\n2. No functionality is broken by the styling changes\\n3. Design maintains visual hierarchy and color-coded meanings\\n4. Changes are minimal and focused on contrast fixes only\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign\\n- Changes to other pages\\n- Functionality modifications\\n- Theme system overhaul\\n\\n## Analysis of Current Issues\\nBased on the SelfImprovementDashboard code review, potential problem areas:\\n\\n1. **Lines 266-267**: `bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\"` - This should be correct\\n2. **Lines 433-434**: Card with conditional background (`bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'light\'} text={autoApplyEnabled ? \'white\' : \'dark\'}`) - Light background with dark text should be readable\\n3. **Lines 451**: `bg-dark` class usage in auto-apply warning section\\n\\nThe issue might be in CSS overrides or Bootstrap theme customization that\'s causing text to appear black on dark backgrounds despite proper Bootstrap classes being used.\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- User is referring to the SelfImprovementDashboard component (Improve page)\\n- Issue is with CSS/styling, not functional behavior\\n- Bootstrap framework is being used correctly in most places\\n- Problem may be in CSS overrides or theme customization\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n1. Analyze current styling and identify specific contrast violations\\n2. Fix styling issues using appropriate Bootstrap classes or custom CSS\\n3. Test readability across different states (auto-apply on/off, different card states)\\n4. Ensure accessibility compliance\\n5. Verify no regressions in functionality or other visual elements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011TFtLkpjAUrteE5ssD2dWn', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Milestone 1: Analysis and Architecture\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone focuses on understanding the current RecoveryDashboard implementation and identifying specific CSS/styling issues causing readability problems. The testing strategy ensures we thoroughly analyze and document all readability issues before implementing fixes.\n\n## Test Strategy Summary\n- **Focus**: Analysis and Documentation Testing\n- **Target**: SelfImprovementDashboard component readability issues\n- **Approach**: Visual regression testing + accessibility compliance testing\n- **Coverage Goal**: 100% of UI components analyzed for readability\n\n## Testing Categories\n\n### 1. Visual Analysis Tests\n**Purpose**: Identify and document all readability issues in current implementation\n\n#### Task 1.1: Component Rendering Tests\n- **Type**: Unit Tests\n- **Target**: SelfImprovementDashboard component\n- **Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library + @testing-library/jest-dom\n- **Coverage**: \n  - Render component in different states (auto-apply on/off)\n  - Snapshot tests to capture current styling\n  - Verify all expected elements are present\n\n#### Task 1.2: CSS Class Application Tests  \n- **Type**: Unit Tests\n- **Target**: Bootstrap class application\n- **Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Test `bg="dark"` with `text="white"` combinations\n  - Test conditional background classes\n  - Verify proper CSS class assignments\n\n### 2. Accessibility Compliance Tests\n**Purpose**: Measure current accessibility violations and establish baseline\n\n#### Task 2.1: Contrast Ratio Testing\n- **Type**: Integration Tests  \n- **Target**: All text/background combinations\n- **Framework**: Jest + axe-core + @testing-library/jest-dom\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Test WCAG AA compliance (4.5:1 contrast ratio)\n  - Identify specific elements failing contrast requirements\n  - Document current contrast ratios for baseline\n\n#### Task 2.2: Screen Reader Testing\n- **Type**: Integration Tests\n- **Target**: Component accessibility tree\n- **Framework**: Jest + @testing-library/jest-dom\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Verify proper ARIA labels exist\n  - Test semantic HTML structure\n  - Validate screen reader compatibility\n\n### 3. Cross-Browser Visual Tests\n**Purpose**: Identify browser-specific rendering issues affecting readability\n\n#### Task 3.1: Multi-Browser Screenshot Tests\n- **Type**: E2E Tests\n- **Target**: SelfImprovementDashboard rendering\n- **Framework**: Playwright with visual comparisons\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Chrome, Firefox, Safari rendering\n  - Light/dark mode variations\n  - Different viewport sizes\n\n#### Task 3.2: CSS Override Detection Tests\n- **Type**: Integration Tests\n- **Target**: CSS cascade and specificity issues\n- **Framework**: Playwright with CSS inspection\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Identify conflicting CSS rules\n  - Document CSS specificity problems\n  - Test Bootstrap theme overrides\n\n### 4. State-Based Readability Tests  \n**Purpose**: Test readability across all component states\n\n#### Task 4.1: Interactive State Testing\n- **Type**: Integration Tests\n- **Target**: Component state changes\n- **Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library + user-event\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Auto-apply toggle on/off states\n  - Different card background states\n  - Modal open/closed states\n  - Alert visibility states\n\n#### Task 4.2: Dynamic Content Readability\n- **Type**: Integration Tests\n- **Target**: Dynamically rendered content\n- **Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library\n- **Coverage**:\n  - Table content with various data\n  - Badge colors with different statuses\n  - Alert messages with different types\n\n## Test Data Requirements\n\n### Baseline Documentation\n- Current component screenshots in all states\n- List of all CSS classes applied to text elements\n- Contrast ratio measurements for each text/background pair\n- Browser compatibility matrix\n- Accessibility audit results\n\n### Test Fixtures\n- Sample improvement data for table rendering\n- Different auto-apply states for conditional styling testing\n- Mock data for various alert/badge scenarios\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Analysis Completeness (100% Coverage)\n- ✅ All UI components analyzed for readability\n- ✅ All text/background combinations documented\n- ✅ All CSS class applications verified\n- ✅ All accessibility violations identified\n\n### Documentation Quality\n- ✅ Specific contrast ratios measured and recorded\n- ✅ Browser-specific issues documented\n- ✅ CSS override conflicts identified\n- ✅ Baseline screenshots captured\n\n### Test Infrastructure\n- ✅ Visual regression testing setup functional\n- ✅ Accessibility testing pipeline established\n- ✅ Cross-browser testing capability verified\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n### Risk: Incomplete Issue Identification\n**Mitigation**: Multi-layered testing approach (unit + integration + E2E) ensures no readability issues are missed\n\n### Risk: False Positive Accessibility Violations\n**Mitigation**: Manual verification of automated accessibility tool results to ensure real issues are identified\n\n### Risk: Browser-Specific Issues Not Detected\n**Mitigation**: Cross-browser testing matrix covers all major browsers and versions\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Test Environment Setup\n- Node.js test environment with jsdom for component testing\n- Playwright for cross-browser E2E testing\n- axe-core integration for accessibility testing\n- Visual regression baseline establishment\n\n### Continuous Integration\n- Tests run on every commit to catch regressions\n- Visual diff reports generated for review\n- Accessibility compliance reports generated\n- Browser compatibility matrix updated\n\n## Deliverables\n\n1. **Comprehensive Issue Documentation** - Detailed list of all readability problems\n2. **Visual Regression Test Suite** - Automated tests to prevent future regressions  \n3. **Accessibility Compliance Report** - WCAG compliance status and violations\n4. **CSS Analysis Report** - Documentation of styling conflicts and overrides\n5. **Browser Compatibility Report** - Cross-browser readability status\n\n## Next Steps\nAfter completing this analysis and testing phase, results will be passed to TDD Coordinator for test implementation, then to Frontend Captain for actual readability fixes based on the documented issues.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011TFtLkpjAUrteE5ssD2dWn', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260114_215308.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260114_215308.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'sta