{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:53:33", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-32138cf1-1309-44b5-9218-070029c66e42', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 1: Analysis and Investigation - Identify all readability issues and their root causes in the SelfImprovementDashboard component",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AP9iwt9fvRAdhjWaUgrsW2', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AP9iwt9fvRAdhjWaUgrsW2', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: British Brass Band Achievements\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis project extends the existing Ensemble achievements system by adding a new \\"BRASS_BAND\\" achievement category. This follows an **extension pattern** - adding new content to an existing, well-structured system without modifying core architecture.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Plugin/Extension pattern for achievement categories\\n**Approach Rationale**: The existing achievements system is well-designed with clear enum-based categories and a list-based achievement registry. We simply extend these existing structures.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Current Stack (Maintained)\\n- **Backend**: Python with typed dataclasses for Achievement models\\n- **Frontend**: React with Bootstrap for UI components\\n- **State Management**: Props-based filtering in React components\\n- **API**: Existing achievement endpoints (no changes needed)\\n\\n### No New Dependencies Required\\nThe existing stack fully supports this extension.\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n**1. AchievementCategory Enum** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Has SKA and other categories\\n- **Change**: Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` enum value\\n\\n**2. ACHIEVEMENTS List** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Contains Achievement objects for existing categories\\n- **Change**: Add 15 new Achievement objects for BRASS_BAND category\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n**3. AchievementsDashboard** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`)\\n- **Filter Dropdown**: Add brass_band option with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n- **getCategoryBadge Function**: Handle brass_band category styling\\n- **Fun Facts Section**: Optionally add brass band trivia\\n\\n### Component Interaction Flow\\n```\\nUser selects \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n    \\u2193\\nAchievementsDashboard filters by category=\\"brass_band\\"\\n    \\u2193\\nAPI returns achievements with category BRASS_BAND\\n    \\u2193\\nUI displays brass band achievements with proper badges\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.py          # MODIFY: Add enum + 15 achievements\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementsDashboard.jsx  # MODIFY: Add filter + badge\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement Object (Existing Pattern)\\n```python\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,  # NEW CATEGORY\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Achievement Definitions (15 Total)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Rarity | Points | Trigger Type |\\n|----|------|--------|--------|--------------|\\n| championship_section | Championship Section | LEGENDARY | 200 | total_executions >= 50 |\\n| silver_band | Silver Band | RARE | 50 | consecutive_successes >= 5 |\\n| principal_cornet | Principal Cornet | UNCOMMON | 30 | sub_agents_led >= 3 |\\n| adjudicator | The Adjudicator | RARE | 60 | test_evaluations >= 25 |\\n| test_piece | Test Piece Mastery | UNCOMMON | 25 | iterations_in_task > 10 |\\n| bandroom_practice | Bandroom Practice | COMMON | 15 | total_executions >= 10 |\\n| promotion | Section Promotion | EPIC | 100 | success_rate_improvement |\\n| brass_section_harmony | Brass Section Harmony | RARE | 45 | concurrent_completions |\\n| march_on_stage | March on Stage | COMMON | 10 | first_task_in_project |\\n| quick_march | Quick March | RARE | 40 | task_time < 10s |\\n| hymn_tune_encore | Hymn Tune Encore | UNCOMMON | 35 | recovery_from_failure |\\n| grand_shield | Grand Shield | EPIC | 120 | consecutive_successes >= 25 |\\n| fanfare | Fanfare | RARE | 55 | achievements_in_session >= 5 |\\n| youth_band_graduate | Youth Band Graduate | UNCOMMON | 20 | new_agent_first_10_tasks |\\n| national_finals | National Finals | LEGENDARY | 150 | project_completion |\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API Changes Required**\\n- Existing `/api/achievements` endpoint supports category filtering\\n- Frontend already handles dynamic category data\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Backend Testing\\n1. Verify BRASS_BAND enum exists\\n2. Verify 15 achievements load without errors\\n3. Verify achievement triggering works\\n4. Run existing achievement test suite\\n\\n### Frontend Testing\\n1. Verify brass_band filter appears in dropdown\\n2. Verify filter functionality works\\n3. Verify badge displays correctly\\n4. Verify no console errors\\n\\n### Manual Verification\\n- Load AchievementsDashboard\\n- Select \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n- Verify achievements display with correct icons/badges\\n- Verify at least one achievement can trigger\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend (achievements.py)\\n1. Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to AchievementCategory enum\\n2. Add 15 Achievement objects to ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. Verify file imports correctly\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend (AchievementsDashboard.jsx)\\n1. Add brass_band to category filter dropdown\\n2. Update getCategoryBadge function\\n3. Optionally add fun facts\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Integration Testing\\n1. Run existing tests\\n2. Manual verification\\n3. Commit changes\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Trigger Condition Compatibility\\n**Impact**: New trigger conditions might not work with existing tracker\\n**Mitigation**: Use only existing trigger condition types\\n\\n### Risk 2: Frontend Filter Inconsistency\\n**Impact**: Filter might not match backend category name\\n**Mitigation**: Ensure exact string match \\"brass_band\\"\\n\\n## Key Implementation Decisions\\n\\n1. **Enum Value**: Use `brass_band` (lowercase with underscore) matching existing pattern\\n2. **Icon**: Use \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary icon since cornet emoji unavailable\\n3. **Trigger Conditions**: Reuse existing types, no new event tracking\\n4. **Points Range**: Follow existing scale based on rarity\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. \\u2705 BRASS_BAND in AchievementCategory enum\\n2. \\u2705 15 achievements in ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. \\u2705 brass_band filter works in UI\\n4. \\u2705 getCategoryBadge handles brass_band\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests pass\\n6. \\u2705 No console errors in frontend\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012j798hLWgYossfTVoncisU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012j798hLWgYossfTVoncisU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Readability Fix - Improve Page\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Vision**: Fix the unreadable text on the \\"Improve\\" page (SelfImprovementDashboard component) where black text appears on dark backgrounds, making it nearly impossible to read.\\n\\n**Problem**: Users report that the Improve page has severe readability issues with black text on dark backgrounds, creating a poor user experience and making the interface unusable in some areas.\\n\\n**Solution**: Identify and fix all instances of poor contrast between text and background colors to ensure proper readability across all UI elements.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Core Requirements\\n1. **Readability Fix**: Ensure all text on the Improve page is readable with proper contrast\\n2. **Bootstrap Consistency**: Maintain Bootstrap theme consistency while fixing contrast issues\\n3. **Dark Mode Compatibility**: Ensure fixes work properly in both light and dark mode contexts\\n4. **Accessibility**: Meet WCAG guidelines for text contrast (minimum 4.5:1 ratio for normal text)\\n\\n### Specific Issues to Address\\n1. **Card Backgrounds**: Review all Card components with `bg=\\"dark\\"` and ensure text is white/light\\n2. **Alert Styling**: Ensure Alert components have proper text contrast\\n3. **Badge Colors**: Verify Badge components maintain readability\\n4. **Auto-Apply Toggle**: Check styling of the toggle switch and associated text\\n5. **Table Content**: Ensure table text is readable against backgrounds\\n6. **Modal Content**: Verify modal text readability\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing Bootstrap theme\\n- Cannot break existing functionality\\n- Must preserve current color scheme intent (danger/warning/success indicators)\\n- Should use Bootstrap\'s built-in text color classes where possible\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. All text on the Improve page is readable with adequate contrast\\n2. No functionality is broken by the styling changes\\n3. Design maintains visual hierarchy and color-coded meanings\\n4. Changes are minimal and focused on contrast fixes only\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign\\n- Changes to other pages\\n- Functionality modifications\\n- Theme system overhaul\\n\\n## Analysis of Current Issues\\nBased on the SelfImprovementDashboard code review, potential problem areas:\\n\\n1. **Lines 266-267**: `bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\"` - This should be correct\\n2. **Lines 433-434**: Card with conditional background (`bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'light\'} text={autoApplyEnabled ? \'white\' : \'dark\'}`) - Light background with dark text should be readable\\n3. **Lines 451**: `bg-dark` class usage in auto-apply warning section\\n\\nThe issue might be in CSS overrides or Bootstrap theme customization that\'s causing text to appear black on dark backgrounds despite proper Bootstrap classes being used.\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- User is referring to the SelfImprovementDashboard component (Improve page)\\n- Issue is with CSS/styling, not functional behavior\\n- Bootstrap framework is being used correctly in most places\\n- Problem may be in CSS overrides or theme customization\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n1. Analyze current styling and identify specific contrast violations\\n2. Fix styling issues using appropriate Bootstrap classes or custom CSS\\n3. Test readability across different states (auto-apply on/off, different card states)\\n4. Ensure accessibility compliance\\n5. Verify no regressions in functionality or other visual elements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XaifAzDNAMiC2DykbMLwoa', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Milestone 1: Analysis and Investigation\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone focuses on identifying all readability issues and their root causes in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The goal is thorough analysis and documentation of contrast violations before implementing fixes.\n\n## Test Categories\n\n### 1. Visual Regression Tests\n**Purpose**: Detect current readability issues and establish baseline\n**Tools**: Playwright for visual testing, axe-core for accessibility\n\n#### Test Tasks:\n\n**Task 1.1: Screenshot Baseline Tests**\n- Create screenshots of SelfImprovementDashboard in all states:\n  - Auto-apply disabled (light mode)\n  - Auto-apply enabled (danger mode) \n  - Modal dialogs open\n  - Different card states\n  - Loading states\n- Store as baseline for regression detection\n- Coverage: Visual state coverage\n\n**Task 1.2: Contrast Ratio Analysis**\n- Programmatically test all text elements for WCAG AA compliance (4.5:1 ratio)\n- Test color combinations:\n  - bg-dark with default text\n  - bg-danger with white text\n  - bg-light with dark text\n  - Card headers and bodies\n  - Table content\n  - Modal content\n- Identify specific failing elements\n- Coverage: Accessibility compliance\n\n### 2. Component Integration Tests\n**Purpose**: Verify component rendering and state management\n**Tools**: React Testing Library, Jest\n\n#### Test Tasks:\n\n**Task 2.1: Bootstrap Class Application Tests**\n- Test that correct Bootstrap classes are applied:\n  - `bg="dark" text="white"` combinations\n  - `bg="danger" text="white"` combinations\n  - `bg="light" text="dark"` combinations\n- Verify conditional styling logic works correctly\n- Test auto-apply toggle state changes\n- Coverage: Component state and styling logic\n\n**Task 2.2: CSS Override Detection Tests**\n- Test for conflicting CSS rules that override Bootstrap classes\n- Check computed styles match expected Bootstrap values\n- Identify custom CSS that may cause contrast issues\n- Test CSS cascade and specificity problems\n- Coverage: Style inheritance and overrides\n\n### 3. User Experience Tests\n**Purpose**: Simulate real user interactions with readability issues\n**Tools**: Playwright E2E tests\n\n#### Test Tasks:\n\n**Task 3.1: User Journey Readability Tests**\n- Navigate through all sections of SelfImprovementDashboard\n- Attempt to read all text elements\n- Test in different browser environments\n- Simulate different display settings (zoom, font size)\n- Coverage: End-to-end user experience\n\n**Task 3.2: Cross-Browser Contrast Tests**\n- Test rendering in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\n- Test on different operating systems\n- Check for browser-specific rendering issues\n- Verify font rendering consistency\n- Coverage: Browser compatibility\n\n### 4. Accessibility Audit Tests\n**Purpose**: Comprehensive accessibility evaluation\n**Tools**: axe-core, manual testing\n\n#### Test Tasks:\n\n**Task 4.1: Automated Accessibility Testing**\n- Run axe-core accessibility tests\n- Check for WCAG violations beyond contrast\n- Test keyboard navigation\n- Verify screen reader compatibility\n- Coverage: Full accessibility compliance\n\n**Task 4.2: Manual Accessibility Testing**\n- Manual review with screen reader software\n- Test with high contrast mode enabled\n- Verify color-blind accessibility\n- Test with system dark mode\n- Coverage: Real-world accessibility scenarios\n\n## Test Infrastructure\n\n### Setup Requirements\n- Playwright for browser automation\n- Jest + React Testing Library for component tests\n- axe-core for accessibility testing\n- Color contrast analyzer tools\n- Multiple browsers for cross-platform testing\n\n### Test Data\n- Component props for different states\n- Mock data for dashboard content\n- Various viewport sizes\n- Different theme configurations\n\n### Coverage Goals\n- **Visual Coverage**: 100% of UI states captured\n- **Contrast Testing**: All text/background combinations analyzed\n- **Component Coverage**: All rendering paths tested\n- **Accessibility Coverage**: WCAG AA compliance verified\n- **Browser Coverage**: Chrome, Firefox, Safari tested\n\n## Expected Deliverables\n\n### 1. Readability Issues Report\n- Comprehensive list of all contrast violations\n- Screenshots showing problematic areas\n- Specific CSS classes/elements affected\n- WCAG compliance analysis\n\n### 2. Root Cause Analysis\n- Identification of CSS overrides causing issues\n- Bootstrap class conflicts\n- Theme customization problems\n- Browser-specific rendering issues\n\n### 3. Test Suite Implementation\n- Automated contrast testing\n- Visual regression tests\n- Component integration tests\n- Accessibility audit tests\n\n### 4. Baseline Documentation\n- Current state screenshots\n- Contrast ratio measurements\n- Accessibility audit results\n- Browser compatibility matrix\n\n## Success Criteria\n- ✅ All readability issues identified and documented\n- ✅ Root causes clearly understood\n- ✅ Comprehensive test suite implemented\n- ✅ Baseline established for future regression testing\n- ✅ Ready to proceed to fix implementation phase\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **False Positives**: Manual review of automated contrast findings\n- **Browser Differences**: Test on multiple browsers/OS combinations\n- **Dynamic Content**: Test all possible component states\n- **Theme Dependencies**: Test with different Bootstrap theme configurations\n\nThis analysis phase ensures we thoroughly understand the problem scope before implementing fixes, preventing incomplete solutions and regression issues.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XaifAzDNAMiC2DykbMLwoa', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260114_215333.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260114_215333.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
