{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:54:44", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9aca62d7-a8d2-452d-8aea-c8139375f846', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 2: Frontend UI Updates - Add brass_band category to filter dropdown with \\ud83c\\udfba icon, update getCategoryBadge function in AchievementsDashboard.jsx",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/brass_band_achievements_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015CfM4GhnxtkhLTgJ3NoRyW', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0178sVJkYBZQRdfccdKzAvtu', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/brass_band_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015CfM4GhnxtkhLTgJ3NoRyW', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: British Brass Band Achievements\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis project extends the existing Ensemble achievements system by adding a new \\"BRASS_BAND\\" achievement category. This follows an **extension pattern** - adding new content to an existing, well-structured system without modifying core architecture.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Plugin/Extension pattern for achievement categories\\n**Approach Rationale**: The existing achievements system is well-designed with clear enum-based categories and a list-based achievement registry. We simply extend these existing structures.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Current Stack (Maintained)\\n- **Backend**: Python with typed dataclasses for Achievement models\\n- **Frontend**: React with Bootstrap for UI components\\n- **State Management**: Props-based filtering in React components\\n- **API**: Existing achievement endpoints (no changes needed)\\n\\n### No New Dependencies Required\\nThe existing stack fully supports this extension.\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n**1. AchievementCategory Enum** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Has SKA and other categories\\n- **Change**: Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` enum value\\n\\n**2. ACHIEVEMENTS List** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Contains Achievement objects for existing categories\\n- **Change**: Add 15 new Achievement objects for BRASS_BAND category\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n**3. AchievementsDashboard** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`)\\n- **Filter Dropdown**: Add brass_band option with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n- **getCategoryBadge Function**: Handle brass_band category styling\\n- **Fun Facts Section**: Optionally add brass band trivia\\n\\n### Component Interaction Flow\\n```\\nUser selects \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n    \\u2193\\nAchievementsDashboard filters by category=\\"brass_band\\"\\n    \\u2193\\nAPI returns achievements with category BRASS_BAND\\n    \\u2193\\nUI displays brass band achievements with proper badges\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.py          # MODIFY: Add enum + 15 achievements\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementsDashboard.jsx  # MODIFY: Add filter + badge\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement Object (Existing Pattern)\\n```python\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,  # NEW CATEGORY\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Achievement Definitions (15 Total)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Rarity | Points | Trigger Type |\\n|----|------|--------|--------|--------------|\\n| championship_section | Championship Section | LEGENDARY | 200 | total_executions >= 50 |\\n| silver_band | Silver Band | RARE | 50 | consecutive_successes >= 5 |\\n| principal_cornet | Principal Cornet | UNCOMMON | 30 | sub_agents_led >= 3 |\\n| adjudicator | The Adjudicator | RARE | 60 | test_evaluations >= 25 |\\n| test_piece | Test Piece Mastery | UNCOMMON | 25 | iterations_in_task > 10 |\\n| bandroom_practice | Bandroom Practice | COMMON | 15 | total_executions >= 10 |\\n| promotion | Section Promotion | EPIC | 100 | success_rate_improvement |\\n| brass_section_harmony | Brass Section Harmony | RARE | 45 | concurrent_completions |\\n| march_on_stage | March on Stage | COMMON | 10 | first_task_in_project |\\n| quick_march | Quick March | RARE | 40 | task_time < 10s |\\n| hymn_tune_encore | Hymn Tune Encore | UNCOMMON | 35 | recovery_from_failure |\\n| grand_shield | Grand Shield | EPIC | 120 | consecutive_successes >= 25 |\\n| fanfare | Fanfare | RARE | 55 | achievements_in_session >= 5 |\\n| youth_band_graduate | Youth Band Graduate | UNCOMMON | 20 | new_agent_first_10_tasks |\\n| national_finals | National Finals | LEGENDARY | 150 | project_completion |\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API Changes Required**\\n- Existing `/api/achievements` endpoint supports category filtering\\n- Frontend already handles dynamic category data\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Backend Testing\\n1. Verify BRASS_BAND enum exists\\n2. Verify 15 achievements load without errors\\n3. Verify achievement triggering works\\n4. Run existing achievement test suite\\n\\n### Frontend Testing\\n1. Verify brass_band filter appears in dropdown\\n2. Verify filter functionality works\\n3. Verify badge displays correctly\\n4. Verify no console errors\\n\\n### Manual Verification\\n- Load AchievementsDashboard\\n- Select \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n- Verify achievements display with correct icons/badges\\n- Verify at least one achievement can trigger\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend (achievements.py)\\n1. Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to AchievementCategory enum\\n2. Add 15 Achievement objects to ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. Verify file imports correctly\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend (AchievementsDashboard.jsx)\\n1. Add brass_band to category filter dropdown\\n2. Update getCategoryBadge function\\n3. Optionally add fun facts\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Integration Testing\\n1. Run existing tests\\n2. Manual verification\\n3. Commit changes\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Trigger Condition Compatibility\\n**Impact**: New trigger conditions might not work with existing tracker\\n**Mitigation**: Use only existing trigger condition types\\n\\n### Risk 2: Frontend Filter Inconsistency\\n**Impact**: Filter might not match backend category name\\n**Mitigation**: Ensure exact string match \\"brass_band\\"\\n\\n## Key Implementation Decisions\\n\\n1. **Enum Value**: Use `brass_band` (lowercase with underscore) matching existing pattern\\n2. **Icon**: Use \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary icon since cornet emoji unavailable\\n3. **Trigger Conditions**: Reuse existing types, no new event tracking\\n4. **Points Range**: Follow existing scale based on rarity\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. \\u2705 BRASS_BAND in AchievementCategory enum\\n2. \\u2705 15 achievements in ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. \\u2705 brass_band filter works in UI\\n4. \\u2705 getCategoryBadge handles brass_band\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests pass\\n6. \\u2705 No console errors in frontend\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0178sVJkYBZQRdfccdKzAvtu', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# British Brass Band Achievements - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** British Brass Band Achievements Expansion  \\n**Project ID:** 29b97d5e  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nExpand the existing Ensemble achievements system with a new \\"British Brass Band\\" category inspired by NABBA (North American Brass Band Association) and the British brass band tradition. These achievements celebrate the rich heritage of brass banding including competitions, sections, traditional instrumentation, and contest culture.\\n\\n## Background: NABBA & British Brass Bands\\n\\nNABBA (North American Brass Band Association) promotes British-style brass bands in North America since 1983. Key characteristics:\\n- **Contest Culture**: Championships with adjudicators scoring bands on test pieces\\n- **Section System**: Bands compete in divisions based on ability (Championship, Honor, Challenge, etc.)\\n- **Traditional Instrumentation**: Cornets, flugelhorn, tenor horns, baritones, euphoniums, trombones, tubas, percussion\\n- **Silver Band Tradition**: Many bands carry \\"Silver Band\\" in their name\\n- **Community Focus**: Youth bands, community bands, university bands\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Add New Category**: Create `BRASS_BAND` achievement category (parallel to existing `SKA` category)\\n2. **Achievement Content**: Add 10-15 British brass band themed achievements\\n3. **UI Updates**: Add brass band category to filter dropdown in AchievementsDashboard\\n4. **Maintain Consistency**: Follow existing achievement patterns for rarity, triggers, and points\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Backend Changes** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`):\\n- Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to `AchievementCategory` enum\\n- Add 10-15 new `Achievement` objects to the `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n- Include variety of rarities (common through legendary)\\n\\n**Frontend Changes** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`):\\n- Add brass_band category to filter dropdown with icon (\\ud83c\\udfba)\\n- Add brass_band to `getCategoryBadge` function\\n- Update \\"Brass/Band Facts\\" section or add separate fun facts\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- New API endpoints (using existing endpoints)\\n- Database schema changes (existing schema supports new category)\\n- New UI components beyond filter updates\\n\\n## Achievement Definitions\\n\\n### Theme Guidelines\\nBritish brass band achievements should reference:\\n- Contest/competition terminology (adjudicator, test piece, draw, sections)\\n- Instrumentation (cornets, euphoniums, tubas, percussion)\\n- Band traditions (Silver Bands, marching, community, youth development)\\n- Famous brass band pieces and composers\\n- Section rankings and promotions\\n- NABBA-specific events and culture\\n\\n### Proposed Achievements (10-15)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Description | Rarity | Points | Icon |\\n|----|------|-------------|--------|--------|------|\\n| `championship_section` | Championship Section | Achieved legendary status with 50+ successful tasks | LEGENDARY | 200 | \\ud83c\\udfc6 |\\n| `silver_band` | Silver Band | First agent to maintain 100% success rate across 5 tasks | RARE | 50 | \\ud83e\\udd48 |\\n| `principal_cornet` | Principal Cornet | Led 3+ sub-agents to successful completion in one task | UNCOMMON | 30 | \\ud83c\\udfba |\\n| `adjudicator` | The Adjudicator | Evaluated and passed judgment on 25+ test results | RARE | 60 | \\ud83d\\udccb |\\n| `test_piece` | Test Piece Mastery | Completed a particularly challenging task (>10 iterations) | UNCOMMON | 25 | \\ud83d\\udcdc |\\n| `bandroom_practice` | Bandroom Practice | Executed 10 tasks total (like rehearsal makes perfect) | COMMON | 15 | \\ud83c\\udfb5 |\\n| `promotion` | Section Promotion | Improved success rate from <50% to >90% | EPIC | 100 | \\u2b06\\ufe0f |\\n| `brass_section_harmony` | Brass Section Harmony | Multiple agents completed tasks simultaneously | RARE | 45 | \\ud83c\\udfb6 |\\n| `march_on_stage` | March on Stage | Completed first task of a new project | COMMON | 10 | \\ud83d\\udeb6 |\\n| `quick_march` | Quick March | Completed a task in under 10 seconds | RARE | 40 | \\u26a1 |\\n| `hymn_tune_encore` | Hymn Tune Encore | Recovered from failure and succeeded (like a well-loved encore) | UNCOMMON | 35 | \\ud83d\\ude4f |\\n| `grand_shield` | Grand Shield | Completed 25 consecutive successful tasks | EPIC | 120 | \\ud83d\\udee1\\ufe0f |\\n| `fanfare` | Fanfare | Triggered 5+ achievements in a single session | RARE | 55 | \\ud83d\\udcef |\\n| `youth_band_graduate` | Youth Band Graduate | New agent class completed its first 10 tasks | UNCOMMON | 20 | \\ud83c\\udf93 |\\n| `national_finals` | National Finals | Participated in project completion (full lifecycle) | LEGENDARY | 150 | \\ud83c\\udfc5 |\\n\\n### Achievement Implementation Details\\n\\n```python\\n# Example achievement definition pattern (for Development Manager reference)\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks - polished performance!\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Existing Patterns**: Must follow existing achievement definition pattern\\n2. **Category Enum**: Add to existing `AchievementCategory` enum\\n3. **Frontend Consistency**: Match existing category badge/filter patterns\\n4. **Trigger Conditions**: Use existing trigger condition types where possible\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 `BRASS_BAND` category added to `AchievementCategory` enum\\n2. \\u2705 10-15 brass band achievements added to `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n3. \\u2705 Frontend filter dropdown includes brass_band with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n4. \\u2705 `getCategoryBadge` function handles brass_band category\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests continue to pass\\n6. \\u2705 Achievements unlock correctly when conditions are met\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n### Backend File to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`\\n\\n### Frontend File to Modify\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Run existing achievement tests to ensure no regressions\\n- Manually verify brass_band filter works in UI\\n- Verify at least one achievement can be triggered\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n\\n1. **Icon Choice**: Using \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary brass band icon since cornet emoji isn\'t widely available\\n2. **Trigger Conditions**: Reusing existing trigger types (consecutive_successes, total_executions, etc.)\\n3. **Points Balance**: Following existing points range (10-200) based on rarity\\n4. **No New Events**: Not adding new event types to activity tracker\\n\\n## Fun Facts for UI (Optional Enhancement)\\n\\nConsider adding to the fun facts section:\\n> **Did you know?** British-style brass bands date back to the early 1800s and originated in the industrial areas of Northern England. The standard brass band uses 25-30 players on cornets, horns, baritones, euphoniums, trombones, and tubas - no woodwinds allowed! The Black Dyke Band (founded 1855) is one of the oldest and most successful brass bands in the world. NABBA has been bringing this tradition to North America since 1983! \\ud83c\\udfba\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Implementation  \\n**Next Step:** Delegate to Development Manager for implementation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016N1zwhFU6TYSirQ3H7sHZG', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md', 'content': '# Frontend Tasks - Milestone 2: Frontend UI Updates\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone adds brass_band category support to the AchievementsDashboard component, including filter dropdown and badge styling updates.\n\n**Component**: `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`  \n**Total Tasks**: 3  \n**Estimated Complexity**: Simple\n\n## User Flow\n1. User opens AchievementsDashboard\n2. User sees "Brass Band 🎺" option in category filter dropdown\n3. User selects "Brass Band" filter\n4. Dashboard displays only brass_band category achievements\n5. Each brass_band achievement shows proper badge styling\n\n---\n\n## Task List\n\n### Task 1: Add brass_band to Filter Dropdown\n**ID**: FE-M2-001  \n**Component**: AchievementsDashboard.jsx  \n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Description**:\nAdd brass_band option to the category filter dropdown with trumpet icon (🎺).\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Dropdown includes option: "Brass Band 🎺" with value "brass_band"\n- [ ] Option appears in alphabetical order with other categories\n- [ ] Selecting filter triggers component state update\n- [ ] Filter correctly queries backend for category="brass_band"\n- [ ] No console errors when selecting brass_band filter\n\n**Implementation Notes**:\n- Locate existing category filter dropdown (likely using Bootstrap dropdown or native select)\n- Add new option element matching existing pattern\n- Ensure value matches backend enum: "brass_band" (lowercase with underscore)\n- Use 🎺 emoji icon for visual consistency\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Test Requirements**:\n- Unit test: Verify brass_band option renders in dropdown\n- Unit test: Verify selecting brass_band updates component state/filter\n- Integration test: Verify filtering by brass_band calls API with correct parameter\n- Visual test: Verify emoji renders correctly across browsers\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Update getCategoryBadge Function\n**ID**: FE-M2-002  \n**Component**: AchievementsDashboard.jsx  \n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Description**:\nUpdate getCategoryBadge helper function to handle brass_band category with appropriate styling.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] getCategoryBadge function handles "brass_band" case\n- [ ] Returns badge component with proper styling (Bootstrap badge or similar)\n- [ ] Badge text displays "Brass Band" (capitalized, user-friendly)\n- [ ] Badge color distinguishes from other categories (suggest: gold/amber theme)\n- [ ] Badge includes 🎺 emoji icon\n\n**Implementation Notes**:\n- Locate getCategoryBadge function (likely a switch/case or object lookup)\n- Add brass_band case matching existing pattern\n- Suggested styling: `badge bg-warning text-dark` or custom brass-themed color\n- Format: "🎺 Brass Band" or "Brass Band 🎺" (match existing icon placement)\n\n**Dependencies**: \n- Task FE-M2-001 (filter must exist for testing)\n\n**Test Requirements**:\n- Unit test: getCategoryBadge("brass_band") returns expected badge component\n- Unit test: Badge contains correct text and styling classes\n- Visual test: Badge is visually distinct from ska, general, and other categories\n- Accessibility test: Badge has proper contrast ratio for readability\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Verify End-to-End Filter Flow\n**ID**: FE-M2-003  \n**Component**: AchievementsDashboard.jsx  \n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Description**:\nIntegration test and manual verification of complete brass_band filter functionality.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Selecting brass_band filter displays only brass_band achievements\n- [ ] Achievement cards display brass_band badges correctly\n- [ ] No JavaScript errors in console\n- [ ] Filter state persists during session (if applicable)\n- [ ] "Clear filter" or "All categories" resets to show all achievements\n\n**Implementation Notes**:\n- This is primarily a testing/verification task\n- May identify edge cases from Tasks 1-2\n- Verify behavior matches existing category filters (ska, etc.)\n\n**Dependencies**: \n- Task FE-M2-001 (filter dropdown)\n- Task FE-M2-002 (badge function)\n\n**Test Requirements**:\n- Integration test: Select brass_band filter → verify API call → verify filtered results\n- Manual test: Load dashboard, select brass_band, verify UI updates\n- Regression test: Verify other category filters still work correctly\n- Cross-browser test: Verify functionality in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\n\n---\n\n## Component Structure Reference\n\n### Expected File Structure\n```javascript\n// src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx\n\nconst getCategoryBadge = (category) => {\n  switch(category) {\n    case \'ska\':\n      // existing ska badge\n    case \'brass_band\':  // NEW CASE\n      return <Badge bg="warning" text="dark">🎺 Brass Band</Badge>;\n    // ... other cases\n  }\n};\n\n// In render/return:\n<Form.Select onChange={handleCategoryFilter}>\n  <option value="all">All Categories</option>\n  <option value="ska">SKA 🎷</option>\n  <option value="brass_band">Brass Band 🎺</option>  {/* NEW OPTION */}\n  {/* ... other options */}\n</Form.Select>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests (Jest + React Testing Library)\n1. **Filter Dropdown Rendering**\n   - Test brass_band option exists in dropdown\n   - Test option has correct value attribute\n\n2. **getCategoryBadge Function**\n   - Test brass_band returns correct badge component\n   - Test badge has expected classes and text\n\n3. **State Management**\n   - Test selecting brass_band updates filter state\n   - Test filter state triggers correct API call\n\n### Integration Tests\n1. **Full Filter Flow**\n   - Mount component → select brass_band → verify filtered achievements\n   - Mock API response with brass_band achievements\n\n2. **Badge Display**\n   - Render achievement with category="brass_band" → verify badge displays\n\n### Manual Testing Checklist\n- [ ] Load AchievementsDashboard in browser\n- [ ] Verify brass_band appears in dropdown\n- [ ] Select brass_band filter\n- [ ] Verify only brass_band achievements display\n- [ ] Verify badges render correctly\n- [ ] Check console for errors\n- [ ] Test on mobile viewport\n- [ ] Test with browser emoji support (Chrome, Firefox, Safari)\n\n---\n\n## Technical Assumptions\n\n**Framework**: React (existing)  \n**UI Library**: Bootstrap (based on architecture patterns)  \n**State Management**: Props/hooks (no Redux mentioned in architecture)  \n**API Client**: Existing achievement endpoint with category filter parameter  \n\n**Styling Approach**:\n- Use Bootstrap badge component (`bg-warning` or custom class)\n- Gold/amber theme to differentiate from SKA (likely blue/purple)\n- Ensure WCAG AA contrast compliance\n\n**Browser Support**:\n- Modern browsers with emoji support\n- Trumpet emoji 🎺 is widely supported (Unicode 6.0)\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies and Order\n\n```\nFE-M2-001 (Filter Dropdown)\n    ↓\nFE-M2-002 (Badge Function)\n    ↓\nFE-M2-003 (Integration Verification)\n```\n\n**Total Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours (including tests)\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n**Definition of Done**:\n1. ✅ brass_band option in filter dropdown\n2. ✅ Selecting filter displays only brass_band achievements\n3. ✅ getCategoryBadge handles brass_band category\n4. ✅ Badges render with correct styling\n5. ✅ All unit tests pass\n6. ✅ All integration tests pass\n7. ✅ No console errors\n8. ✅ Code follows existing component patterns\n9. ✅ Accessible (keyboard navigation, screen readers)\n\n---\n\n## Notes for TDD Coordinator\n\n**Critical Details**:\n- Category value must be **exact string match**: `"brass_band"` (lowercase, underscore)\n- Badge styling should be **visually distinct** from existing categories\n- Follow **existing component patterns** - no architectural changes\n- **Test-driven approach**: Write tests first, then implement\n\n**Potential Edge Cases**:\n- Empty state: No brass_band achievements exist yet (backend pending)\n- API error handling: Backend returns 500 when fetching brass_band\n- Browser emoji rendering: Fallback if 🎺 not supported\n\n**Coordination Notes**:\n- Backend Milestone 1 must be complete before full integration testing\n- Can develop/test UI with mocked data independently\n- Verify backend enum value matches frontend filter value\n\n---\n\n**Status**: Ready for TDD Implementation  \n**Next Step**: Hand off to TDD Coordinator for test-driven implementation\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016N1zwhFU6TYSirQ3H7sHZG', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2_20260114_215444.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2_20260114_215444.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 94.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.3\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
